-- title:
--   Hecke eigenspace of Tₚ J₁(M) at a primitive form
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $\varepsilon$ be a Dirichlet character mod $M$ with complex values, and let $g$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form for $\Gamma_1(M)$ which is primitive for $\varepsilon$, i.e. an eigenform with character $\varepsilon$ whose eigenpacket $(n\mapsto \mathrm{qCoeff}\,g\,n,\ n\mapsto\varepsilon(n))$ does not occur at any proper divisor $M'$ of $M$. Let $p$ be a prime, and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) (for every prime $\ell$ the inputs `HeckeInputsOneAlong` over an algebraic closure of $\mathbf Q$, and for every $d$ coprime to $M$ a diamond automorphism of the function field of $X_1(M)$ together with its base change to the geometric function field) and [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54) (the geometric Hecke and diamond generators commute pairwise). Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $K$ a field of characteristic zero that is a $\mathbf Z_p$-algebra, $R$ a commutative ring with an injective ring homomorphism $toC:R\to\mathbf C$ and a ring homomorphism $\psi:R\to K$, and $b,e:\mathbf N\to R$ with $toC(b_\ell)=\mathrm{qCoeff}\,g\,\ell$ and $toC(e_\ell)=\varepsilon(\ell)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Give $J_1(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the geometric function field of $X_1(M)$ the module structure over $\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne}=\mathbf Z[X_{\text{primes}\sqcup\mathbf N}]$ furnished by [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129), write $T=T_p(J_1(M))$ for the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_1(M)$ with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$, and let $\Lambda$ be any ring homomorphism from the $\mathbf Q_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbf Q_p}(\mathbf Q_p\otimes T)$ generated by the Hecke action to $K$ such that $\Lambda(c)=c$ for $c\in\mathbf Z_p$ (via the respective algebra maps) and such that, for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, $\Lambda(T_\ell)\psi(e_\ell)=\psi(b_\ell)$ and $\Lambda(\langle\ell\rangle)\psi(e_\ell)=1$. Then, inside $V=K\otimes_{\mathbf Z_p}T$, the intersection over all $t\in\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne}$ of the kernels of $\hat t-\Lambda(t)\cdot\mathrm{id}$, where $\hat t$ is the base change to $K$ of the action of $t$ on $T$, is non-zero, and it meets the $K$-span of $\{\hat t\,y-\Lambda(t)\,y: t\in\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne},\ y\in V\}$ in $0$.
--
--   This is the statement that at the eigenvalue packet of a primitive form the simultaneous Hecke eigenspace in the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_1(M)$ is non-trivial and splits off from the augmentation submodule generated by the operators $\hat t-\Lambda(t)$; it is the semisimplicity input that makes the eigenspace a well-behaved direct summand. It is used in the analysis of the inertia action on this eigenspace, namely in producing an element of an inertia subgroup whose effect on a vector is not contained in that span.
